{"prompt": "what does this do?\n\n```typescript\nexport function groupBy<T, K extends keyof T>(\n  records: readonly T[],\n  field: K,\n): Map<T[K], T[]> {\n  const grouped = new Map<T[K], T[]>();\n  for (const record of records) {\n    const key = record[field];\n    const bucket = grouped.get(key);\n    if (bucket) bucket.push(record);\n    else grouped.set(key, [record]);\n  }\n  return grouped;\n}\n```", "response": "It group a list of records by a field. It walks the records once, appending each into the bucket named by its key, which is a single pass rather than one scan per group."}
